# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Only VITE_-prefixed vars reach the client.

# POST target for the /free-playbook capture form. This is the form that
# enrols a contact into the 5-email nurture sequence, so point it at the ESP
# list (or a serverless function in front of it), not at a generic inbox.
# Left empty, the form succeeds locally and logs a warning instead of sending.
VITE_PLAYBOOK_ENDPOINT=

# Third-party services, all declared in src/config/vendors.js. Every one of
# them is inert while its id is empty: the vendor is treated as not existing,
# no script is created whatever a visitor consents to, and it stays out of the
# generated cookie policy. That is deliberate — the site ships and behaves
# correctly with none of these filled in.

# Google Tag Manager container. Carries GA4, Meta and TikTok, so it sits
# behind the marketing category rather than analytics.
VITE_GTM_ID=

# Microsoft Clarity project id. Heatmaps, click tracking and session replay,
# and it syncs with Microsoft Advertising — so it is also behind marketing.
VITE_CLARITY_ID=

# Tawk.to property id. Essential, but loads on click rather than on consent,
# so a visitor who rejected analytics can still ask for help.
VITE_TAWK_ID=

# Where the /contact form POSTs. Left empty, the form does NOT fake success:
# it hands the message to the visitor's own mail client, pre-filled, and says
# so. Nothing is ever silently dropped.
VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=
